1
00:00:00.120 --> 00:00:00.953
Hey, everybody.

2
00:00:00.953 --> 00:00:02.460
Welcome to Rollback.

3
00:00:02.460 --> 00:00:06.360
Rollback is my way of introducing powerful,

4
00:00:06.360 --> 00:00:07.193
enlightening,

5
00:00:07.193 --> 00:00:08.850
and evergreen conversations

6
00:00:08.850 --> 00:00:12.270
from the prehistoric pre-video days of the podcast

7
00:00:12.270 --> 00:00:15.540
right here on YouTube for the very first time.

8
00:00:15.540 --> 00:00:19.497
Conversations like this one from July of 2015

9
00:00:19.497 --> 00:00:22.350
with former NFL star, David Carter,

10
00:00:22.350 --> 00:00:26.280
AKA the 300 pound vegan.

11
00:00:26.280 --> 00:00:29.730
Like most athletes, David grew up eating tons of meat,

12
00:00:29.730 --> 00:00:32.400
fully adhering to the conventional mythology

13
00:00:32.400 --> 00:00:35.070
that in order to become muscle,

14
00:00:35.070 --> 00:00:37.530
you must consume muscle.

15
00:00:37.530 --> 00:00:39.720
But as his career matured,

16
00:00:39.720 --> 00:00:42.000
David became plagued by a variety

17
00:00:42.000 --> 00:00:44.089
of persistent, chronic injuries,

18
00:00:44.089 --> 00:00:46.950
including arthritis and tendonitis,

19
00:00:46.950 --> 00:00:49.290
ailments he simply could not overcome

20
00:00:49.290 --> 00:00:50.640
that left him sidelined

21
00:00:50.640 --> 00:00:52.980
despite the best sports medicine

22
00:00:52.980 --> 00:00:55.515
and rehabilitative resources of the NFL

23
00:00:55.515 --> 00:00:57.570
at his disposal.

24
00:00:57.570 --> 00:00:58.403
And so,

25
00:00:58.403 --> 00:01:01.560
through a series of rather improbable events

26
00:01:01.560 --> 00:01:03.870
in February of 2014,

27
00:01:03.870 --> 00:01:06.300
David made this rather radical

28
00:01:06.300 --> 00:01:07.770
and quite controversial decision,

29
00:01:07.770 --> 00:01:11.970
which was to adopt a 100% plant-based diet.

30
00:01:11.970 --> 00:01:13.170
As a result,

31
00:01:13.170 --> 00:01:15.960
to the great surprise of his coaches,

32
00:01:15.960 --> 00:01:17.646
his trainers, his teammates,

33
00:01:17.646 --> 00:01:21.750
every single one of those nagging, persistent injuries

34
00:01:21.750 --> 00:01:24.300
mysteriously corrected themselves

35
00:01:24.300 --> 00:01:27.450
and ultimately vanished altogether.

36
00:01:27.450 --> 00:01:30.120
All his numbers in the weight room went up.

37
00:01:30.120 --> 00:01:32.280
He found himself quicker, more agile,

38
00:01:32.280 --> 00:01:34.170
and more responsive than ever.

39
00:01:34.170 --> 00:01:36.176
And perhaps most important to David,

40
00:01:36.176 --> 00:01:41.040
no living thing had to die in order for him to thrive.

41
00:01:41.040 --> 00:01:42.810
It's a truly special exchange

42
00:01:42.810 --> 00:01:44.400
with an exceptional human being

43
00:01:44.400 --> 00:01:48.245
that explores a typical day in the life of the NFL,

44
00:01:48.245 --> 00:01:51.660
it's a peek into the typical NFL diet,

45
00:01:51.660 --> 00:01:53.700
what he eats now on a daily basis,

46
00:01:53.700 --> 00:01:55.770
and tons more.

47
00:01:55.770 --> 00:01:58.380
I sincerely hope you enjoy our discussion

48
00:01:58.380 --> 00:02:00.081
and look forward to your thoughts

49
00:02:00.081 --> 00:02:02.523
in the comments section below.

